{
  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "totalVI 的输入是 RNA 与蛋白的 UMI 计数矩阵，与你提供的 RNA 和蛋白均为 UMI counts 一致。",
      "basis": "KG_GROUNDED",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 2,
          "quote": "The input to totalVI consists of the matrices of RNA and protein unique molecular identifier (UMI) counts (Fig."
        }
      ],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "totalVI 明确支持 CITE-seq 的批次整合任务，因此两个 CITE-seq 批次属于其声明支持的范围。",
      "basis": "KG_GROUNDED",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 3,
          "quote": "totalVI can be used for disparate analysis tasks including joint dimensionality reduction, dataset integration (with and without missing proteins), protein background correction, estimation of correlations between genes and/or proteins, and differential expression testing."
        }
      ],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "批次或供体等分类协变量是用于整合的可选输入，而不是强制要求。",
      "basis": "KG_GROUNDED",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 2,
          "quote": "Categorical covariates such as experimental batch or donor are optional inputs used for integrating datasets and referred to henceforth as “batch”."
        }
      ],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "提醒：来源允许不同抗体 panel 以及部分 scRNA-seq 子集，因此不能把“每个细胞都必须测到蛋白”当作硬性输入门槛。",
      "basis": "CAUTION_CONTEXT",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 6,
          "quote": "Input datasets can have different antibody panels, and a subset can be scRNA-seq datasets (i.e., without proteins)."
        }
      ],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "提醒：缺失蛋白的整合按批次索引建模，并假设所有批次共享同一组基因；这不代表对任意缺失模式都有无条件的填补保证。",
      "basis": "CAUTION_CONTEXT",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 7,
          "quote": "As any single batch may correspond to an experiment that used a different protein panel (or no proteins in the case of a scRNA-seq experiment), the missingness of protein features depends on the batch index sn. Further, suppose all batches share the same set of genes."
        }
      ],
      "context_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "clarification": null
}
